The Interactions Rig block's `Locomotor` carries two Interaction SDK comfort effects, `SmoothMovementTunneling` and `WallPenetrationTunneling`. Each is a driver script in `Oculus.Interaction.Locomotion` plus a `TunnelingEffect` (namespace `Oculus.Interaction`) that draws a full-view quad 0.3 m in front of the centre eye (`ZTest Always`, transparent queue) with a feathered circular hole. `Configure Building Blocks` disables every Behaviour in `Oculus.Interaction.Locomotion`, so it switched off the drivers, which normally hide the quads every frame, but left the `TunnelingEffect` components running with their serialized defaults: the wall-penetration one shows a 60Â° hole in a grey (0.547) mask permanently. That is the "fisheye": the hub panel was hidden behind it except through the hole, and the site was visible only through the hole. Editor verification missed it three times because every screenshot came from a separate preview camera, which saw the quads edge-on as a "black plate" beside the foreman.

