## In the headset

Revised October 22, after the fourth build (the tunnel removed): one site, everything in front, real scale, words you can read, days you can see. Decisions K45 to K48; work order WO-L8.

- You start in your room, in full passthrough, and can see and talk to the others. Nothing is drawn but a panel within arm's reach: the day, the connection, and one button, Go to the site.
- Touch it. The site materializes around you where you stand: a wave runs outward from your feet; just behind its front everything is glowing wire and blueprint lines over the room, then the surfaces fill in, until the room is gone and the sky closes over you. You do not move; the site is built around you.
- You stand on the road. The trench runs across in front of you, 6 m away. The three crews work in front of you at real size: the pipe crew in the middle, the excavator to the right, the backfill loader to the left, nearer or farther as the real gaps between them change. Machines crawl as they work; you never move. The stake by each crew shows its real station. The rest of the site runs off to the horizon on both sides.
- Look at a crew for two seconds and you have walked over to it: its foreman greets you or says what is going on, and the host treats you as standing there. Whatever anyone says shows in a speech bubble over their head while it plays. A Log button on your wrist opens a panel in front of you with the last twenty lines, the day and the clock state; grab it and leave it anywhere.
- Each day the sun crosses the sky; at the day boundary the light dims to dusk and the new day opens with its number in front of you. When the wall falls you see it fall in front of you; when the foremen argue, they meet in front of you.
- Back on your left wrist dissolves the site into your room.

## Principles

1. **Claims, not conclusions.** A voice says what the speaker sees, feels or wants. It never names the situation code, the cause in manual terms, the days lost, the response options, or what to do. LOB-Game's PM event lines already work this way ("A trench wall came down. The pipe crew has stopped.").
2. **Every claim is checkable by another seat.** A foreman's number is a rate, a day or a station that Plan can find on the LOB or Rules can run through the front-page rule. A claim nobody can check is noise.
3. **Speakers are partial.** Each foreman argues for his crew and blames the other crew or the schedule. Both are partly right; the team reconciles them with the LOB and the manual.
4. **Problems hide in normal lines.** Deviations are never announced. The excavation foreman whose order never arrived sounds cheerful about a good digging day. Only a Site player who knows what the office ordered hears the problem, and only Plan can tell Site what was ordered.
5. **Each voice reaches one seat.** Foremen are heard in the headset only (or on `site.html`). The PM and the radio play on the Plan laptop; the PM also appears as the hub standee for the morning brief. Rules hears nothing; Rules has paper. Whatever matters crosses the table in someone's own words.
6. **Once only.** A line plays once. Listen near a crew replays that crew's last line. No transcript is shown during play; the end-of-stage change log lists who said what and when.
7. **No verdict voices.** No line responds to whether a decision was good. The PM pushes against holds, demobilizations and purchases whatever the outcome; the end line states facts.

| K45 | One site, one button: the three crews work in front of the player at real scale with the pipe crew in the middle and the others at distances that follow their real gaps (compressed), the player never moves, looking at a crew for 2 s is walking over to it (`moveTo`) | Bryan, October 22: three buttons made him expect three places; everything can happen in one site in front of him | `LEVEL1.md`, WO-L8 |
| K46 | Speech is shown as well as heard: a bubble over the speaker while a line plays and a grabbable log panel the player opens in front of themselves | Bryan, October 22: without the text it is hard to understand what is going on | WO-L8 |
| K47 | Days are visible in the headset: the sun crosses the sky each day and the day boundary is a dusk with the day number shown; never fully dark, no flashes under 0.3 s | Bryan, October 22, like the calendar on the Plan page | WO-L8 |
| K48 | Machines, workers and props are real size (excavator 9.5 m by 3.2 m to the cab roof, crane 12 m by 3.8 m, loader 6 m by 3.2 m, pipe 0.3 m, workers 1.8 m) and rest on the ground by the ground height function | Bryan, October 22: the equipment was tiny and floating | WO-L8 |
using LOBOver.XR;
using UnityEngine;

namespace LOBOver.Play
{
    public sealed class LogButton : MonoBehaviour
    {
        public SpeechLog log;
        private InteractionSurface surface;
        private void OnEnable() { surface = GetComponent<InteractionSurface>(); surface.Selected += Press; }
        private void OnDisable() { if (surface != null) surface.Selected -= Press; }
        private void Press(Vector3 ignored) => log.Toggle();
    }
}
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using LOBOver.World;
using LOBOver.XR;
using TMPro;
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.UI;

namespace LOBOver.Play
{
    public sealed class SpeechLog : MonoBehaviour
    {
        public HostVoice voice;
        public HostWorldPresenter presenter;
        public WarpController warp;
        public XRRig rig;
        public Transform panel;
        public TMP_Text header, history;
        public ScrollRect scroll;
        public Material cardMaterial;
        // WO-L8 items 5-6, metres / seconds / retained lines.
        public const int LineLimit = 20, BubbleLimit = 2;
        public const float Width = 0.5f, Height = 0.35f, Ahead = 1, BelowEye = 0.15f;
        public const float Letters = 0.015f, BubbleLetters = 0.02f, BubbleDistance = 10, AboveHead = 0.4f, TailSeconds = 2;
        public sealed class Entry { public int Day; public string Crew, Speaker, Text; }
        public IReadOnlyList<Entry> Lines => lines;
        public int BubbleCount => bubbles.Count;
        public bool Open => panel.gameObject.activeSelf;
        private readonly List<Entry> lines = new List<Entry>();
        private readonly List<Bubble> bubbles = new List<Bubble>();
        private sealed class Bubble { public Transform Root; public CrewRig Crew; public float Until; }
        private bool placed;
        private string run;
        private void OnEnable() { voice.Speaking += Show; voice.Cleared += Clear; }
        private void OnDisable() { voice.Speaking -= Show; voice.Cleared -= Clear; ClearBubbles(); }
        private void Clear()
        {
            ClearBubbles();
            if (run == presenter.connection.RunId) return;
            run = presenter.connection.RunId; lines.Clear(); if (history != null) history.text = "";
        }
        private void ClearBubbles()
        { foreach (var bubble in bubbles) if (bubble.Root != null) Destroy(bubble.Root.gameObject); bubbles.Clear(); }
        private void Show(string speaker, string text, int day, float duration)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text)) return;
            var crewId = HostVoice.CrewId(speaker);
            var name = crewId == "exc" ? "Ray" : crewId == "pipe" ? "Marcus" : crewId == "back" ? "Dana" : speaker;
            var entry = new Entry { Day = day, Crew = crewId, Speaker = name, Text = text };
            lines.Add(entry); if (lines.Count > LineLimit) lines.RemoveAt(0);
            history.text = string.Join("\n\n", lines.Select(line => "Day " + line.Day + "  <color=#" + Colour(line.Crew) + ">" + line.Speaker
                + "</color>\n<noparse>" + line.Text + "</noparse>"));
            Canvas.ForceUpdateCanvases(); scroll.verticalNormalizedPosition = 0;
            var crew = presenter.world.Crew(crewId);
            if (crew == null) return;
            while (bubbles.Count >= BubbleLimit) { Destroy(bubbles[0].Root.gameObject); bubbles.RemoveAt(0); }
            var root = WorldDrawing.Group("Speech_" + name, transform).transform;
            var card = WorldDrawing.Box("Card", root, Vector3.zero, new Vector3(1.25f, 0.32f, 0.012f), cardMaterial);
            Destroy(card.GetComponent<Collider>());
            var label = WorldDrawing.Text("Words", root, new Vector3(0, 0, -0.009f), new Vector2(1.17f, 0.28f), BubbleLetters, presenter.world.assets.font);
            label.richText = true; label.alignment = TextAlignmentOptions.TopLeft;
            var face = label.font.faceInfo; label.fontSize = BubbleLetters * 10 * face.pointSize / Mathf.Max(1, face.capLine);
            label.text = "<color=#" + Colour(crewId) + ">" + name + "</color>\n<color=#FFFFFF><noparse>" + text + "</noparse></color>";
            label.ForceMeshUpdate();
            var height = Mathf.Max(0.14f, label.preferredHeight + 0.05f);
            label.rectTransform.sizeDelta = new Vector2(1.17f, height - 0.04f);
            card.transform.localScale = new Vector3(1.25f, height, 0.012f);
            bubbles.Add(new Bubble { Root = root, Crew = crew, Until = Time.unscaledTime + duration + TailSeconds });
        }
        private static string Colour(string crew)
        {
            var index = Array.IndexOf(WorldUnits.CrewIds, crew);
            return ColorUtility.ToHtmlStringRGB(index < 0 ? Color.white : WorldUnits.CrewColours[index]);
        }
        public void Toggle()
        {
            if (Open) { panel.gameObject.SetActive(false); return; }
            if (!rig.TryHeadPose(out var pose)) return;
            var toPanel = panel.position - pose.position;
            var inView = Vector3.Angle(pose.rotation * Vector3.forward, toPanel) < 60
                && Vector3.Dot(panel.forward, toPanel) > 0;
            if (!placed || !inView)
            {
                var forward = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(pose.rotation * Vector3.forward, Vector3.up).normalized;
                if (forward.sqrMagnitude < 0.1f) forward = Vector3.forward;
                var position = pose.position + forward * Ahead - Vector3.up * BelowEye;
                panel.SetPositionAndRotation(position, Quaternion.LookRotation(position - pose.position)); placed = true;
            }
            panel.gameObject.SetActive(true);
        }
        private void LateUpdate()
        {
            header.text = "Day " + presenter.connection.DisplayDay + "  " + (clock != null && clock.Speed == "slow" ? "Field slow" : "Running");
            if (!warp.InSite || warp.Busy) panel.gameObject.SetActive(false);
            foreach (var bubble in bubbles.ToArray())
            {
                if (bubble.Crew == null || Time.unscaledTime >= bubble.Until)
                { if (bubble.Root != null) Destroy(bubble.Root.gameObject); bubbles.Remove(bubble); continue; }
                bubble.Root.gameObject.SetActive(warp.InSite && !warp.Busy && bubble.Crew.gameObject.activeInHierarchy);
                var bounds = SiteGround.Bounds(bubble.Crew.Foreman);
                bubble.Root.position = new Vector3(bounds.center.x, bounds.max.y + AboveHead, bounds.center.z);
                bubble.Root.rotation = Quaternion.LookRotation(bubble.Root.position - rig.ViewEye.position);
                bubble.Root.localScale = Vector3.one * (Vector3.Distance(bubble.Root.position, rig.ViewEye.position) / BubbleDistance);
            }
        }
        public SiteDayCycle clock;
    }
}

